course: dictionary
lesson: 12816
title: Embedded: fixed firmly inside
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Embedded means fixed firmly inside something else. Think of a stone stuck deep in mud: the stone is embedded in the mud. «The fossil was embedded in the grey rock.» The fossil is inside the rock and held there tightly.
explain: Embedded has other meanings too. In grammar, an embedded clause is a part of a sentence put inside the main sentence, usually between commas. In computing, an embedded video is placed inside a web page. The words around the word show you which meaning it has.
explain: Check the clues. If something is stuck inside something else, embedded probably means that. If a sentence has a part tucked inside it, with commas around it, you are probably looking at grammar. Test your meaning by swapping in "placed firmly inside" and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Embedded means fixed firmly inside something else.
fact: «The shell was embedded deep in the mud.» means the shell was stuck firmly in the mud.
fact: An embedded clause is a part of a sentence put inside the main sentence, usually between commas.
fact: In «The dog, which was muddy, ran into the kitchen», the embedded clause is «which was muddy».
fact: An embedded video or picture is placed inside a web page.
exercise: «The fossil was embedded in the grey rock.» What does embedded mean here? | Painted in bright colours | *Fixed firmly inside something else | Floating on top of the water
exercise: «The dog, which was muddy, ran into the kitchen.» Which words are the embedded clause? | ran into the kitchen | *which was muddy | The dog ran into the kitchen | muddy, ran
exercise: The science lesson has «an embedded video» on a web page. Where is the video? | Lost on the computer desktop | Sold in a shop | Thrown out of the screen | *Placed inside the web page
test: «The arrow was embedded in the tree trunk.» What does embedded mean here? | *Stuck firmly inside the trunk | Carved on the outside of the bark | Blown away by the wind | Hanging loosely from a branch
test: «My brother, who is taller than me, plays football.» Which words are the embedded clause? | taller than me, plays | My brother, who | *who is taller than me | plays football
exam: Which sentence uses embedded to mean placed inside a web page? | *The science video is embedded in our class website. | The science video is embedded in my sock drawer. | The science video is embedded under the table. | The science video was embedded in a cup of tea.
